BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Phoenician Scheme
DTSTART:20250703T231500Z
DTEND:20250704T012000Z
DTSTAMP:20250703T231500Z
UID:tF1E8vpB0H
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nThe story of a family and a fami
 ly business. Benicio del Toro plays tycoon Anatole "Zsa-zsa" Korda\, one o
 f the richest men in Europe\; Mia Threapleton is Sister Liesl\, his daught
 er/a nun\; Michael Cera is Bjorn Lund\, an entomologist.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/cinema/in-theaters/phoenician-scheme
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Familiar Touch
DTSTART:20250703T233000Z
DTEND:20250704T012500Z
DTSTAMP:20250703T233000Z
UID:h9R2UpAfyP
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nRuth Goldman (Broadway legend Kat
 hleen Chalfant) has been living with dementia for some time\, and the time
  has come to place her in an assisted living facility. But while this may 
 seem like the end\, for her it represents something like a new beginning i
 n this poignant\, Venice Film Festival-winning drama.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/cinema/in-theaters/familiar-touch
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art for Everybody
DTSTART:20250704T020000Z
DTEND:20250704T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20250704T020000Z
UID:Rmam4jd1P0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nThomas Kinkade was one of the mos
 t successful artists of his day\, with millions of cozy cottage paintings 
 sold across the U.S. On his passing in 2012\, a newly discovered vault con
 tained a series of darkly themed paintings that reveal a more complicated 
 and troubled man than his most popular works implied.\n\nhttps://www.siff.
 net/cinema/in-theaters/art-for-everybody
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:40 Acres
DTSTART:20250704T021500Z
DTEND:20250704T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20250704T021500Z
UID:46LKkjx1de
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nMusic video veteran R.T. Thorne 
 directs SAG nominee Danielle Deadwyler (The Piano Lesson) in this TIFF sen
 sation\, a speculative fiction thriller about a Black family in a starved\
 , post-civil war near future who must defend their farm from invading cann
 ibals.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/40-acres
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
